{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And concerning the doubling, etc.</b> It alludes to two things: to the doubling and to the change — that the second dream did not come like the first dream, ״seven cows,״ etc., for then he would think that the impression of the first dream made an impact on his mind and arose upon his bed twice. Therefore the dream came in a new order: ״seven ears of grain,״ etc. This comes to teach that the matter is certain and from before Elohim the dream came to him, and not a false imagining." "And His saying <b>and Elohim hastens, etc.</b> — meaning, that the dream came doubled in a single night and did not come in two separate, distant times, is to tell him that the time is near and not to distant times will it relate."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:35.779196731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}